      "id": "origins-earth-human-history-s044-p00530",
      "source_en": "We know that tin was traded by sea from Northern Europe by the Phoenicians sailing through the Strait of Gibraltar from about 450 BC, and before this along overland trade routes to the Fertile Crescent. 7 And as tin was scarce in the ancient world, it would have commanded a high price. Copper ore, on the other hand, was more widely distributed, and our planet has made it available to us through a particularly intriguing process.",
